00:00:05.510 --> 00:00:07.349 align:start position:0%
safety standards are on the agenda this  month as ministers responsible for  competitiveness in the eu meet in  brussels  unions looking to modernize safety  requirements for personal protection  equipment and devices using cables for  transport like cable cars and chair  lifts the aims to strengthen controls  without placing a heavy burden or costs  on industry  smart regulation and the management of  customs risks to ease trade are on the  agenda too  ministers will also try to agree on a  broad outline for reform of the travel  package directive the arrival of online  travel services has changed the way the  sector operates and the council wants to  make sure the protection for travelers  is kept up to date  the reform would also aim to cut costs  and red tape to small and medium  enterprises which make up much of the  travel sector  and as the european space agency sets a  world first from its rosetta spacecraft  landing a probe on a comet 500 million  kilometers from earth the ministers will  debate the challenges and direction that  eu space policy should take in the  future  italian astronaut luca parmitano will  share his experience on the  international space station with the  council
 

